WEBVTT

00:00:57.678 --> 00:01:01.307
could actually set gender equality
back by 15 years.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.685
I know what you must be thinking.

00:01:04.685 --> 00:01:06.395
This is a total buzzkill.

00:01:06.395 --> 00:01:08.106
(Laughter)

00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:10.149
So the climate challenge
is not big enough,

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:13.277
you’re adding solving gender
equality to the equation?

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:15.154
I get the feeling.

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:17.615
But the good news is, if we do it right,

00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:21.327
we have a unique chance to advance
both the climate agenda

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:22.954
and gender equality.

00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:24.539
How?

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:27.041
By being intentional about it.

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:31.337
But first, let's go back to that 15-year
setback risk I mentioned.